---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'connect', text: 'Connect the model' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'edit', text: 'Read the edit' },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Quickstart"
  headings={headings}
  source="site/src/pages/docs/quickstart.astro"
>
  <div class="breadcrumb">
    Get started <span>/</span> <span>Quickstart</span>
  </div>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Connect a model and edit a weight</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Point a model at the weights. WSM keeps a change when the loss goes down.
    </p>
    <h2 id="connect">Connect the model</h2>
    <Code
      code={`git clone https://github.com/thoriqakbar0/wsm.git
cd wsm
python3 -m pip install -e packages/python
export WSM_TEACHER_URL="https://example.invalid"
export WSM_TEACHER_MODEL="your-model-id"
export WSM_TEACHER_API_KEY="your-key"
wsm run "Improve signed addition. Inspect the weights and test your changes." \\
  --task addition --output runs/addition`}
      lang="bash"
      themes={{ light: 'github-light', dark: 'github-dark' }}
    />
    <h2 id="edit">Read the edit</h2>
    <p>The model sends one command at a time.</p>
    <Code
      code={`{"action":"inspect","tensor":"output.weight","indices":[0,1]}
{"action":"edit","edits":[{"tensor":"output.weight","index":0,"value":1}]}`}
      lang="json"
      themes={{ light: 'github-light', dark: 'github-dark' }}
    />
    <p>WSM keeps the edit when the loss goes down.</p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
